+
+Not run (not mine / inert): `make check` (gate — scheduler's job; its extra
+targets are unchanged by this task), `make test-acceptance-go`, Playwright
+suites beyond the task grep, `make protect` (nothing protected changed;
+`harness/protected.sha256` untouched).
+
+## Open issues
+
+1. **Dependency sanction follow-up** — the five indirect github.com modules
+   above are committed without being in `allow_deps` (guard doesn't scan
+   `// indirect` lines). Planner should add them to T-101's `allow_deps` and
+   harden `extractGoDep` (strip trailing `// indirect`) in a harness task so
+   the tripwire is enforced by the guard, not just the packet.
+2. **Could not delete `migrations/.gitkeep`** — `git rm`/`rm`/`mv` are
+   denied in this environment's shell allowlist. It remains tracked (0
+   bytes, harmless: the dir is no longer empty and sqlc ignores it). A
+   maintainer can drop it in any later commit.
+3. **Test filename cosmetic** —
+   `internal/store/scratch_tamper_test.go` was suggested for rename to
+   `filelayout_test.go`; same rename-denied reason it keeps its name. The
+   test itself is permanent (pins the A-104 on-disk layout assumption), not
